    <Placemark>
      <name>Ein Gedi (עין גדי)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<h3>Ein Gedi (עין גדי)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 04. Chalcolithic Period (-4500 to -3300 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Spring Cave Capture</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Judean Hills</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.4 Summary (Pages 54)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (04. Chalcolithic Period):</b></p>
<p>A Chalcolithic temple complex demonstrating a strong connection to the natural springs in its vicinity. The proximity to these springs suggests their cultic significance and use during this period.</p>]]></description>
